al ghosts be removed geometrically or suppressed sufficiently to leave reliable low-energy gauge scattering?","connectionCount":0,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0050"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4bebd8a18c0c7e0dc291320f631e74c7d0657a1eae814a5eec1a9227db10504b","title":"Can a four-dimensional N = 1 heterotic compactification have vanishing superpotential after strong gauge dynamics and all relevant instanton sectors are included? Appendix C tests whether gauge and worldsheet sectors alone can settle this question.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0051"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4b99f1136f864e2624968c9710ecd8041fa71f4d66de5ce134f7b445a02d10c6","title":"Can assumptions behind a unitary black-hole Page curve exclude global symmetries beyond AdS/CFT, and what connects the success of Euclidean gravitational entropy calculations to holographic UV completion?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0058"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4befc5f7d5154a9b4cad28c59af8648993255de5076ca3876d70a8ed62aaf33b","title":"What group-theoretical mechanism makes axion-like S-fold deformations flat, how are they interpreted in five dimensions, and can it generate nonsupersymmetric deformations of the N = 4, SO(4)-symmetric S-fold that remain perturbatively stable in four-dimensional supergravity?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0068"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4bea2236adce2a83cf3c451f430db2b31ccbb60826ec94caf64e9a0ca2613854","title":"Can charged-scalar CFT correlation functions and their relaxation poles imply weak gravity conjecture conditions for hyperscaling violating (HSV) and Kerr-Newman-AdS (KNA) black holes, particularly near extremality?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0072"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"